I now have enough current information to build this. The latest stable stack is Spring Cloud Gateway 4.3.5 (June 2026, part of the 2025.0 release train). I'll build a production-ready gateway acting as both an OAuth2 Resource Server (validating JWTs) and an OAuth2 Client, with Keycloak as the authorization server.

# Production-Ready Spring Cloud Gateway with Keycloak JWT Security

## Architecture Overview

The gateway will act as both an **OAuth2 Resource Server** (validating incoming Bearer tokens) and route to downstream services. A key security note from the latest releases: The X-Forwarded-* and Forwarded header functionality is disabled by default — if you require it, set `spring.cloud.gateway.server.webflux.trusted-proxies` to a Java regex specifying the proxies whose headers you trust.

```
Client → [Spring Cloud Gateway :8080] → Service A / Service B / Service C
              ↓ validates JWT
         [Keycloak :8443]
```

